<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><br>【Sendai Airport Access Line】</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1920" height="1440" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-1920x1440.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-8225 size-full" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-1920x1440.jpg 1920w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-1280x960.jpg 1280w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-768x576.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/20230222_130706-1-380x285.jpg 380w" sizes="(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>Connects Sendai Airport and Sendai Station in approximately 25 minutes (local train).<br><br>Fare: 660 yen for adults (between Sendai Station and Sendai Airport Station)</p>
</div></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.senat.co.jp/en/top" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai Airport Access Line </a></div>
</div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading"></h2>



<div class="wp-block-group alignwide"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow">
<h2 id="anc-pass" class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Great Value Passes</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-sendai-area-pass.png" alt="sendai-area-pass" class="wp-image-461 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-sendai-area-pass.png 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-sendai-area-pass-768x432.png 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-sendai-area-pass-380x214.png 380w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The Sendai Area Pass: </h2>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">the more you ride, the more you save.</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As of 1st April 2017, the unlimited travel ticket for foreign tourists, Sendai Area Pass, is on sale. This cheap and convenient pass allows you a day of unlimited travel on the Loople Sendai, Sendai City subway lines and buses, and JR trains in the area. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can also receive discounts on entry fees to Zuihoden and Sendai City Museum, among other locations, and other special services. For details, please see the website.</p>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://sendaitravelpass.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai Area Pass  </a></div>
</div>



<div style="height:43px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img decoding="async" width="1600" height="1579" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/marugoto_pass_logo-1.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5445 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/marugoto_pass_logo-1.jpg 1600w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/marugoto_pass_logo-1-1280x1263.jpg 1280w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/marugoto_pass_logo-1-768x758.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/marugoto_pass_logo-1-1536x1516.jpg 1536w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/marugoto_pass_logo-1-380x375.jpg 380w" sizes="(max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The &#8220;Sendai Marugoto Pass&#8221; allows you unlimited travel around Sendai and vicinity</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The pass is good for a two-day period and allows pass-holders unlimited rides on trains and buses. You can travel anywhere in Sendai as well as major sightseeing spots such as Akiu Onsen, Matsushima or Yamadera Temple.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Purchase Until March 13&nbsp; Adults 2,720 yen / Children 1,350 yen</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">From March 14: Adults 2,930 yen / Children 1,470 yen</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Effective period of pass 2 days</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">●Where you can purchase the pass: </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;&#8221;Midori no Madoguchi&#8221;&#8221; (みどりの窓口、ticket office) at all JR stations, reserved seat ticket vending machines at JR Sendai Station, ticket vending machine at Sendai Airport Station, etc.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">●How to use the pass: </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Go through the automatic ticket gate when using JR trains, the subway or the Sendai Airport Line. When using the Loople Sendai bus or other buses, show your pass to the driver when getting off the bus.<br></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">*If you show your Marugoto Pass at the Sendai Tourist Information Center on the 2nd floor of JR Sendai Station, you will receive a coupon booklet containing discount coupons and information on special services.</p>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://sendaitravelpass.jp/2days/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai Marugoto Pass </a></div>
</div>



<div style="height:52px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="634" height="413" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-tep2015_index_top_en.jpg" alt="Tohoku Expressway pass" class="wp-image-469 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-tep2015_index_top_en.jpg 634w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/2-tep2015_index_top_en-380x248.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 634px) 100vw, 634px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Tohoku Expressway pass</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Tohoku Expressway Pass is a special service that allows unlimited use of Tohoku expressways through the ETC system at a flat rate. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The pass user can drive on expressways at a flat rate as many times as they wish for two or more consecutive days up to fourteen days without worrying about additional charges. The service is available via rental car service companies. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For more information, please visit the web site of East Nippon Expressway Company (available in English, Chinese, and Korean).</p>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://en.driveplaza.com/drawari/tohoku_expass/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">  East Nippon Expressway Company   </a></div>
</div>
</div></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<div class="wp-block-group alignwide"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow">
<h2 id="anc-subway" class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Subway &amp; Train</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-subway.jpg" alt="subway" class="wp-image-480 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-subway.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-subway-768x512.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-subway-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Sendai City Subway</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Sendai Subway system runs through Sendai and is convenient for foreigners with announcements made in English. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Especially Sendai Station, Hirosedori Station and Kotodai Koen Station in central Sendai are useful for tourists. You can ride on the subway for free using the Sendai Marugoto Pass.</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.kotsu.city.sendai.jp/english/subway/norikata.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai City Subway </a></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">JR Senseki Line</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">JR Senseki Line provides train services between Aobadori Station (Sendai City) and Ishinomaki Station (Ishinomaki City). Trains runs along the coastal area of Miyagi Prefecture. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can visit JR Sendai Station, the baseball stadium of the Tohoku Rakuten Golden Eagles (Miyaginohara Station), Mitsui Outlet Park Sendai Port (Nakanosakae Station), the Matsushima area (Matsushima Kaigan Station) located outside of Sendai City, and popular tourist sites using this line.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">JR Senzan Line</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">JR Senzan Line provides train services between Sendai Station (Sendai City) and Yamagata Station (Yamagata City, Yamagata Prefecture). </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can visit Sendai Toshogu Shrine (Toshogu Station) which is designated a national Important Cultural Property, Sakunami Onsen (Sakunami Station), and Yamadera (Yamadera Station) which is the popular tourist site in Yamagata using this line.</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.jreast.co.jp/multi/en/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">JR-EAST Official Website</a></div>
</div>
</div></div>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-group alignwide"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow">
<h2 id="anc-buses" class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Buses</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="576" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/loople.jpg" alt="loople" class="wp-image-459 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/loople.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/loople-768x432.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/loople-380x214.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Loople Sendai</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Loople Sendai bus stops at major sightseeing spots in central Sendai. If you purchase a one-day pass, it allows you unlimited rides for the day. If this is your first visit to Sendai, this is an ideal way to see the sights of the city.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>How to use Loople Sendai</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">●It takes about one hour per full circuit.<br>●From the JR Sendai Station West Exit Bus Pool, take the bus from Platform No.16<br>●The first bus from JR Sendai Station departs at 9:00 and the last bus departs at 16:00. Buses run every 20 minutes on weekdays, and every 15 minutes on weekends, holidays, and throughout August.<br>●Get on the bus at the central entrance and get off at the front. When you are getting off the bus, insert your one-day pass into the ticket machine or pay the single fare.<br>●Announcements are made in English.<br>●Change can be made for ¥1,000 bills. Other types of bills cannot be changed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Bus fare</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">■ One-day pass (only good for the Loople Sendai bus)<br>Unlimited rides on the bus for a single day<br>Adults (12 years and older): 630yen<br>Children (under 12 years of age): 320yen<br>■ One-day pass for Loople Sendai and Subway<br>Adults: 920yen<br>Children: 460yen<br>■ Single-ride ticket<br>Adults: 260yen<br>Children: 130yen</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Where to Buy Economical One-day Pass</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">1) JR Sendai Station West Exit Bus Pool Ticket Window<br>2) 16 hotels and accommodation facilities in Sendai City (Tickets are sold at the front desk. Purchases can also be made by non-guests.)<br>3) Facilities along the route of Loople (Sendai Aoba Castle Museum)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Special Offers of One-day Pass for Loople Sendai and Subway</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">■ Sendai Aoba Castle Museum: Adults: 110yen discount on admission fee<br>■ Zuihoden Mausoleum: Adults: 110yen discount on admission fee<br>■ Sendai City Museum: Adults: 110yen discount on admission fee<br><br>…and more!</p>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://loople-sendai.jp/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Loople Sendai Official Website </a></div>
</div>



<div style="height:56px" aria-hidden="true" class="wp-block-spacer"></div>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/bus.jpg" alt="bus" class="wp-image-488 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/bus.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/bus-768x512.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/bus-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Expressway Buses</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you want to visit neighboring prefectures such as Yamagata or Fukushima, or even Tokyo, expressway buses are convenient.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">■ Sendai Station-Miyagi Zao or Togatta leaves from JR Sendai Station West Exit Bus Platform No.33; Travel time: 60 minutes for Miyagi Zao, 75minutes for Togatta; Adult: 1,100 yen for Miyagi Zao, 1,300 yen for Togatta; reservations not necessary</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>■ Sendai Station-Yamagata Station leaves from Sendai Station West Exit Bus Platform No.22; Travel time: 1 hr; Adults: ¥930; reservations not necessary</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>■ Sendai Station-Fukushima Station leaves from Sendai Station West Exit Expressway Bus Center; Travel time: 1 hr; Adults: ¥1100; reservations not necessary</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>＊Winter-only buses<br>■Sendai Station-Yamagata Zao (nonstop service) leaves from JR Sendai Station East Exit Bus Platform No.76; Travel time: 85 minutes; Adult: 1,800 yen; reservation is required: <a href="https://japanbusonline.com/en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://japanbusonline.com/en</a></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><br>Sendai Airport Limousine</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"> ※Services are currently suspended.</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://takeyakotsu.jp/airport-limousine/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai Airport Limousine </a></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Route Buses</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Buses in the Sendai area have English announcements when stopping at major sightseeing spots.<br>There are 242 different bus routes with 48 lines that travel from central Sendai to its outskirts. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The base fare is ¥150 &#8211; ¥180. There is a &#8220;¥120 zone&#8221; where you can ride the bus for only ¥120 within the area. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you use the Sendai Marugoto Pass, you can get on and off the bus anywhere for free.</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.kotsu.city.sendai.jp/english/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Transportation Bureau, City of Sendai<br>(in English) </a></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Sendai Seibu Liner </h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can visit Akiu Onsen easily and quickly using this bus service.(Operated by Takeya Kotsu, bound for Michinoku Park, Kawasaki town)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It is about 40 minutes between Sendai Station and Akiu Sato Center.<br>Fare: Adult 900yen, Child 450yen<br>Bus stop: JR Sendai Station West Exit No.63</p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://takeyakotsu.jp/seibu-liner-fare/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> Sendai Seibu Liner </a></div>
</div>
</div></div>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-group alignwide"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow">
<h2 id="anc-rentalcars" class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Rental Cars</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="681" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-rentalcars-P4177963.jpg" alt="rentalcars" class="wp-image-496 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-rentalcars-P4177963.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-rentalcars-P4177963-768x511.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/1-rentalcars-P4177963-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Rental Cars</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you bring the proper documents with you, you can drive a car in Japan (please check the laws before you leave for Japan). Almost all cars have a car navigation system installed so you can easily find your way around.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Car rental companies<br></strong>Car rental agency counters are located at the Sendai Airport domestic terminal (1st floor). There are also car rental agency offices around JR Sendai Station.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Rent</strong><br>The cost to rent a compact car is about ¥6500 for 24 hours. For each day thereafter, There is an additional ¥5700.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>How to rent a car<br></strong>You can rent a car directly from the agency on the day you arrive. It is recommended that you reserve a car beforehand on the Internet, or other means.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TOYOTA Rent a Car<br>(in English, Chinese, Korean and Thai)<br><a href="https://rent.toyota.co.jp/eng/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://rent.toyota.co.jp/eng/</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">NIPPON RENT-A-CAR<br>(in English)<br><a href="https://www.nipponrentacar.co.jp/english/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://www.nipponrentacar.co.jp/english/index.html</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Times Car Rental<br>(in English, Chinese and Korean)<br><a href="https://www.timescar-rental.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://www.timescar-rental.com/</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">NISSAN Rent a Car<br>(in English, Chinese and Korean)<br><a href="https://nissan-rentacar.com/english/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://nissan-rentacar.com/english/</a></p>
</div></div>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-group alignwide"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow">
<h2 id="anc-taxis" class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Taxis</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1920" height="1280" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/101774-2.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5549 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/101774-2.jpg 1920w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/101774-2-1280x853.jpg 1280w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/101774-2-768x512.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/101774-2-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/101774-2-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Taxis</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;Taxis in Japan are very safe. But most taxi drivers speak only Japanese. Therefore, it is best to point at your destination to the driver.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Fares</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fares differ according to time and distance. The minimum fare for a small-sized taxi is ¥670 and if you take a taxi early in the morning or late at night, there is an extra charge.<br>Taxi fares to major sightseeing spots (small-sized taxi)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>■ Sendai Airport-JR Sendai Station: about ¥5500<br>■ JR Sendai Station-Hirosedori (shopping district): ¥670<br>■ JR Sendai Station-Kokubuncho (entertainment district): ¥670<br>■ JR Sendai Station-Akiu Onsen (hot spring resort): about ¥6000<br>■ JR Sendai Station-Sakunami Onsen (hot spring resort): about ¥7700<br>■ JR Sendai Station-Matsushima: about ¥6300</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Sightseeing Taxi</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Each taxi company has sightseeing courses and offers taxis that will take you around to major sightseeing areas (reservations required).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Inquiries about sightseeing taxi;<br></strong>■Inari Taxi・022-241-1122<br><a href="http://www.inaritaxi.co.jp/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">http://www.inaritaxi.co.jp/</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">■Teisan Cab Sendai・022-231-5151<br><a href="http://www.teisantaxi.jp/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">http://www.teisantaxi.jp/index.html</a><br>(in Japanese)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">■Sendai Taxi Website</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://teigaku-sendai-taxi.com/inbound/">https://teigaku-sendai-taxi.com/inbound/</a></p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="200" height="160" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/bn_STaxiT.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5542"/></figure>
</div></div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-group alignwide"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow">
<h2 id="anc-communitycycle" class="wp-block-heading h-ttl1">Community Cycle</h2>



<div class="wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-top is-largeblock"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="682" src="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/date_bike.jpg" alt="date_bike" class="wp-image-477 size-thumbnail" srcset="https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/date_bike.jpg 1024w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/date_bike-768x512.jpg 768w, https://discoversendai.travel/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/date_bike-380x253.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">”DATE BIKE”, a Community Cycle (Bicycle Sharing) Service</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">DATE BIKE” is a useful bicycle-sharing service which you can rent and return at any cycling port in downtown Sendai. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">＊A Japanese phone number is required to apply for DATEBIKE.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
</div></div>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://docomo-cycle.jp/sendai/en/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"> DATE BIKE Official Website  </a></div>



<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="https://www.city.sendai.jp/jitensha/foreign.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">  Please obey traffic laws  </a></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
            

